          "guid": "mrwvlo4cz7euh6wy",
          "message": {
            "text": "The handshake-failure Commands Log warning is written by the STATUS ROUTE (project request context), not by `codexAppServer.ts` where the failure is detected — `addLogEntry` resolves the project DB from request context, and the session manager runs outside any request, so logging there could misattribute the entry in a multi-project server. The per-dataDir dedup set mirrors `lastMultiConnSignature` one screen up; both flag-clear paths (healthy boot in `codexAppServer.ts`, toggle re-enable in the route below) also clear the dedup so a RECURRING failure logs again.\n",
            "markdown": "The handshake-failure Commands Log warning is written by the STATUS ROUTE (project request context), not by `codexAppServer.ts` where the failure is detected — `addLogEntry` resolves the project DB from request context, and the session manager runs outside any request, so logging there could misattribute the entry in a multi-project server. The per-dataDir dedup set mirrors `lastMultiConnSignature` one screen up; both flag-clear paths (healthy boot in `codexAppServer.ts`, toggle re-enable in the route below) also clear the dedup so a RECURRING failure logs again.\n"
          },
          "locations": [
            {
              "physicalLocation": {
                "artifactLocation": {
                  "uri": "src/routes/channel.ts"
                },
                "region": {
                  "startLine": 145,
                  "endLine": 158,
                  "snippet": {
                    "text": "      lastMultiConnSignature.delete(dataDir);\n    }\n  }\n  // HS-9384 (docs/121 §121.7) — codex app-server drive state: the machine-global\n  // Experimental toggle + a per-project handshake-failure flag. The client hides\n  // the play/prompt surface for codex projects when either says no. A newly\n  // observed failure gets ONE Commands Log warning (written here — project\n  // context — because the session manager runs outside any request).\n  const codexAppServerEnabled = isCodexAppServerEnabled();\n  const codexAppServerFailed = hasCodexAppServerHandshakeFailed(dataDir);\n  if (codexAppServerFailed && !loggedCodexHandshakeFailures.has(dataDir)) {\n    loggedCodexHandshakeFailures.add(dataDir);\n    addLogEntry('trigger', 'incoming', 'Codex app-server handshake failed — drive hidden',\n      'The codex app-server session could not initialize (protocol/version drift or codex not runnable). The play button and codex prompt commands are hidden. Toggle Settings → Experimental → \"Codex app-server drive\" off and on to retry, and check that `codex app-server` works in a terminal.').catch(() => {});"
                  }
                }
              }
            }
          ],
          "properties": {
            "tags": [
              "rationale"
            ]
          },
          "workItemUris": [
            "HS-9384"
          ],
          "partialFingerprints": {
